      en: "The Nini Suhien National Park is a relatively small, yet absolutely vital, highly protected core area nestled directly within the broader Ankasa Conservation Area in the Western Region. This specific zone is heavily guarded to preserve a completely untouched, virgin tract of wet evergreen forest. The terrain is complex, deeply intersected by the Nini and Suhien rivers, which provide a constant, humid microclimate. The park is a crucial scientific baseline, offering researchers a rare glimpse into an ancient, pre-human African rainforest ecosystem, totally free from commercial logging, hunting, or agricultural encroachment. Geography K7 — virgin forest protection."
